title: The open presidential primary

@franchise
title: Who is the Left?
new-page: true

= The primary franchise

An open contest resolves nothing until the alliance defines its electorate.
Every boundary advantages a different kind of organisation: paid-up party
members, movement activists, municipal networks or a public audience attracted
by one candidate.

- @delegates
- @members
- @supporters

@delegates
title: Limit the vote to founding-party delegates
subtitle: Cheap control. SLD and Wiosna machinery dominate a narrow electorate.
on-arrival: primary_electorate = "Founding-party delegates"; primary_franchise_code = 1; primary_turnout = 1400; barons_dissent -= 3; spring_dissent -= 2; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "Delegates receive the presidential ballots"
go-to: access

@members
title: Let members and affiliated movements vote
subtitle: A negotiated electorate; Razem must still trust the common process.
choose-if: razem_cooperation >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: Razem and movement organisers do not trust the common register.
on-arrival: primary_electorate = "Members and affiliated movements"; primary_franchise_code = 2; primary_turnout = 52000; organiser_energy += 2; movement_autonomy += 2; barons_dissent += 2; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The alliance opens one verified membership register"
go-to: access

@supporters
title: Register sympathisers for a public primary
subtitle: Broadest mandate and greatest capture risk.
choose-if: primary_signature_network or local_network >= 45 or turnout_readiness >= 61
unavailable-subtitle: No signature network or local register can verify a public electorate.
on-arrival: primary_electorate = "Registered sympathisers"; primary_franchise_code = 3; primary_turnout = 180000; public_trust += 3; turnout_readiness += 4; media_capacity += 2; barons_dissent += 5; movement_autonomy += 3; news_headline = "Registered sympathisers turn the nomination into a public contest"
go-to: access

@access
title: Who may stand?
new-page: true

= Ballot access

The electorate is **[+ primary_electorate +]**. Now each organisation asks
whether it owns a guaranteed nomination, must find allies across currents, or
can enter through supporter signatures.

- @founders
- @cross_current
- @petitions

@founders
title: Guarantee one place to each founding organisation
subtitle: A controlled core ballot that rewards recognised leaders.
on-arrival: primary_rules = "Founding-organisation nominations"; primary_access_code = 1; party_unity += 2; barons_dissent -= 2; progressives_dissent += 2; labor_dissent += 1; news_headline = "The founders protect their places on the ballot"
go-to: campaign

@cross_current
title: Require endorsements from two political currents
subtitle: Crossover figures enter only if earlier cooperation made sponsorship credible.
choose-if: primary_cross_faction_pact or primary_rules_written or primary_franchise_code >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The currents never agreed how to recognise one another's endorsements.
on-arrival: primary_rules = "Two-current endorsement"; primary_access_code = 2; party_unity += 1; progressives_dissent -= 2; labor_dissent -= 2; barons_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Cross-current endorsements widen the primary"
go-to: campaign

@petitions
title: Use a low supporter-petition threshold
subtitle: Widest field. Prepared organisers gain more than headquarters.
choose-if: primary_franchise_code = 3 and (primary_signature_network or local_network >= 45)
unavailable-subtitle: Only a verified public electorate with a signature network can sustain petitions.
on-arrival: primary_rules = "Supporter-petition access"; primary_access_code = 3; party_unity -= 1; organiser_energy += 3; movement_autonomy += 4; barons_dissent += 5; news_headline = "Supporter petitions place outsiders on the ballot"
go-to: campaign

@campaign
title: How will the primary be fought?
new-page: true

= The primary campaign

Ballot: **[+ primary_rules +]**  
Electorate: **[+ primary_electorate +]**

The arena determines what kind of candidate looks presidential. No later stage
costs resources; once opened, the alliance must finish the contest.

- @television
- @counties
- @issues

@television
title: Hold three televised debates
subtitle: Rewards media-ready candidates and a prepared rapid-response operation.
choose-if: media_capacity >= 20 or primary_tv_ready
unavailable-subtitle: The alliance lacks the production and briefing capacity for national debates.
on-arrival: primary_campaign = "Televised debates"; primary_campaign_code = 1; media_capacity += 2; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Three debates turn the primary into national programming"
go-to: tally

@counties
title: Send the field through county hustings
subtitle: Rewards regional networks, organisers and crossover candidates.
choose-if: local_network >= 45 or primary_signature_network
unavailable-subtitle: Too few county organisations can host and verify the ballot.
on-arrival: primary_campaign = "County hustings"; primary_campaign_code = 2; local_network += 2; turnout_readiness += 2; news_headline = "County hustings test who can organise beyond Warsaw"
go-to: tally

@issues
title: Use workplace, tenant and equality forums
subtitle: Free fallback. Rewards candidates with programme and movement sponsorship.
on-arrival: primary_campaign = "Workplace, tenant and equality forums"; primary_campaign_code = 3; labor_credibility += 1; feminist_trust += 1; organiser_energy += 1; news_headline = "Issue forums make the primary argue about power"
go-to: tally

@tally
title: Count the primary
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.primary_biedron_eligible = 1;
Q.primary_zandberg_eligible = 1;
Q.primary_adb_eligible =
    Q.dziemianowicz_bak_advisor ||
    Q.primary_new_generation ||
    Q.primary_social_slate ||
    Q.primary_union_slate ||
    (
        Q.primary_access_code >= 2 &&
        Q.labor_strength + Q.progressives_strength >= 35
    ) ? 1 : 0;
Q.primary_zukowska_eligible =
    Q.zukowska_advisor ||
    Q.primary_machine_slate ||
    Q.primary_spokesperson_slate ? 1 : 0;
Q.primary_kotula_eligible =
    (
        Q.kotula_advisor ||
        Q.primary_equality_slate ||
        Q.primary_movement_slate
    ) &&
    Q.primary_access_code >= 2 ? 1 : 0;
Q.primary_biejat_eligible =
    (
        Q.biejat_advisor ||
        Q.primary_tenant_slate ||
        Q.primary_union_slate ||
        Q.primary_movement_slate
    ) &&
    Q.primary_access_code >= 2 ? 1 : 0;

let biedron =
    34 + Q.spring_strength * 0.4 - Q.spring_dissent * 0.15 +
    Q.media_capacity * 0.08 + Q.women_support * 0.05;
let zandberg =
    27 + Q.razem_strength * 0.45 - Q.razem_dissent * 0.15 +
    Q.labor_credibility * 0.08 + Q.workers_support * 0.06;
let adb =
    18 + Q.labor_strength * 0.35 + Q.progressives_strength * 0.3 -
    (Q.labor_dissent + Q.progressives_dissent) * 0.08 +
    Q.public_sector_support * 0.08;
let zukowska =
    14 + Q.progressives_strength * 0.35 + Q.barons_strength * 0.15 -
    Q.progressives_dissent * 0.12 + Q.media_capacity * 0.08;
let kotula =
    11 + Q.progressives_strength * 0.35 + Q.spring_strength * 0.25 -
    (Q.progressives_dissent + Q.spring_dissent) * 0.07 +
    Q.feminist_trust * 0.08;
let biejat =
    11 + Q.razem_strength * 0.35 + Q.labor_strength * 0.3 -
    (Q.razem_dissent + Q.labor_dissent) * 0.07 +
    Q.household_security * 0.05;

if (Q.primary_franchise_code == 1) {
    biedron += 14; zandberg += 12; adb += 3;
    zukowska += 10; kotula += 4; biejat += 5;
}
if (Q.primary_franchise_code == 2) {
    biedron += 9; zandberg += 12; adb += 9;
    zukowska += 7; kotula += 8; biejat += 10;
}
if (Q.primary_franchise_code == 3) {
    biedron += 14; zandberg += 7; adb += 11;
    zukowska += 6; kotula += 11; biejat += 8;
}
if (Q.primary_campaign_code == 1) {
    biedron += 12; zandberg += 10; adb += 5;
    zukowska += 11; kotula += 5; biejat += 3;
}
if (Q.primary_campaign_code == 2) {
    biedron += 7; zandberg += 6; adb += 10;
    zukowska += 9; kotula += 7; biejat += 9;
}
if (Q.primary_campaign_code == 3) {
    biedron += 5; zandberg += 12; adb += 13;
    zukowska += 4; kotula += 13; biejat += 13;
}

Q.primary_biedron_weight = Math.max(1, Math.round(biedron));
Q.primary_zandberg_weight = Math.max(1, Math.round(zandberg));
Q.primary_adb_weight = Q.primary_adb_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(adb)) : 0;
Q.primary_zukowska_weight = Q.primary_zukowska_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(zukowska)) : 0;
Q.primary_kotula_weight = Q.primary_kotula_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(kotula)) : 0;
Q.primary_biejat_weight = Q.primary_biejat_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(biejat)) : 0;

const candidates = [
    ["Robert Biedroń", "biedron", Q.primary_biedron_weight],
    ["Adrian Zandberg", "zandberg", Q.primary_zandberg_weight],
    ["Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk", "adb", Q.primary_adb_weight],
    ["Anna-Maria Żukowska", "zukowska", Q.primary_zukowska_weight],
    ["Katarzyna Kotula", "kotula", Q.primary_kotula_weight],
    ["Magdalena Biejat", "biejat", Q.primary_biejat_weight]
].filter(function(candidate) {
    return candidate[2] > 0;
});
Q.primary_total_weight = candidates.reduce(function(total, candidate) {
    return total + candidate[2];
}, 0);
Q.primary_random_roll =
    this.random.uint32() / 4294967296 * Q.primary_total_weight;

// This is a tally, not a weighted lottery. Organisation and campaign choices
// establish each candidate's base; bounded candidate-level turnout variance
// then produces votes for every eligible name. The highest tally wins and the
// displayed shares are calculated from those same counted votes.
const adjusted = candidates.map(function(candidate) {
    const turnoutFactor =
        0.82 + this.random.uint32() / 4294967296 * 0.36;
    return [candidate[0], candidate[1], candidate[2], candidate[2] * turnoutFactor];
}.bind(this));
const adjustedTotal = adjusted.reduce(function(total, candidate) {
    return total + candidate[3];
}, 0);
let allocatedVotes = 0;
const tallied = adjusted.map(function(candidate, index) {
    const votes = index == adjusted.length - 1
        ? Math.max(0, Math.round(Q.primary_turnout) - allocatedVotes)
        : Math.max(
            0,
            Math.floor(
                Math.round(Q.primary_turnout) *
                candidate[3] /
                Math.max(1, adjustedTotal)
            )
        );
    allocatedVotes += votes;
    Q["primary_" + candidate[1] + "_tally"] = votes;
    return [candidate[0], candidate[1], candidate[2], votes];
});
const ordered = tallied.slice().sort(function(left, right) {
    if (right[3] != left[3]) return right[3] - left[3];
    if (right[2] != left[2]) return right[2] - left[2];
    return left[0] < right[0] ? -1 : 1;
});
Q.primary_winner = ordered[0][0];
const runner = ordered[1];
Q.primary_runner_up = runner ? runner[0] : "None";
const winner = ordered[0];
Q.primary_total_votes = tallied.reduce(function(total, candidate) {
    return total + candidate[3];
}, 0);
Q.primary_winner_share = Math.round(
    winner[3] * 1000 / Math.max(1, Q.primary_total_votes)
) / 10;
Q.primary_runner_share = runner
    ? Math.round(runner[3] * 1000 / Math.max(1, Q.primary_total_votes)) / 10
    : 0;
Q.primary_mandate = Math.round(Q.primary_winner_share);

if (Q.primary_mandate >= 45) {
    Q.party_unity += 2;
} else if (Q.primary_mandate < 25) {
    Q.party_unity -= 3;
}
!}
go-to: result_biedron if primary_winner = "Robert Biedroń"; result_zandberg if primary_winner = "Adrian Zandberg"; result_adb if primary_winner = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk"; result_zukowska if primary_winner = "Anna-Maria Żukowska"; result_kotula if primary_winner = "Katarzyna Kotula"; result_biejat if primary_winner = "Magdalena Biejat"

@result_biedron
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.2; primary_active = 0; spring_dissent -= 9; spring_strength += 3; media_capacity += 3; razem_dissent += 4; barons_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Biedroń wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_zandberg
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg"; presidential_candidate_base = 3.2; primary_active = 0; razem_dissent -= 10; razem_strength += 3; labor_credibility += 4; spring_dissent += 6; barons_dissent += 5; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "Zandberg wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_adb
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk"; presidential_candidate_base = 3.0; primary_active = 0; labor_dissent -= 6; progressives_dissent -= 6; labor_credibility += 3; progressive_credibility += 3; public_sector_support += 2; women_support += 2; barons_dissent += 4; spring_dissent += 2; party_unity += 2; news_headline = "Dziemianowicz-Bąk wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_zukowska
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Anna-Maria Żukowska"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.6; primary_active = 0; progressives_dissent -= 6; barons_dissent -= 2; media_capacity += 4; young_support += 2; spring_dissent += 3; razem_dissent += 4; party_unity += 1; news_headline = "Żukowska wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_kotula
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Katarzyna Kotula"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.5; primary_active = 0; spring_dissent -= 6; progressives_dissent -= 5; feminist_trust += 5; women_support += 3; young_support += 3; barons_dissent += 6; razem_dissent += 2; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "Kotula wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_biejat
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.7; primary_active = 0; razem_dissent -= 8; labor_dissent -= 4; organiser_energy += 3; labor_credibility += 3; household_policy_pressure += 2; barons_dissent += 6; spring_dissent += 3; party_unity -= 1; last_policy_stage = "Primary programme"; last_policy_authority = "Lewica party electorate"; last_policy_implementation = "Not enacted"; news_headline = "Biejat wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result
title: A candidate with a constituency
new-page: true

= [+ presidential_candidate +] wins

**[+ presidential_candidate +]** wins a weighted **[+ primary_winner_share +]%**
mandate. **[+ primary_runner_up +]** is the strongest runner-up at
**[+ primary_runner_share +]%**.

Electorate: **[+ primary_electorate +]**  
Ballot access: **[+ primary_rules +]**  
Campaign: **[+ primary_campaign +]**

The result is neither a neutral opinion poll nor a leadership appointment. The
rules chosen by the alliance created the electorate that has now created its
candidate. Losing organisations retain their structures, their dissent and a
record of precisely which rule defeated them.

- @poland_events_2021_2023.independence_2019: Begin the presidential campaign
